## Summary

This is a Spring PetClinic REST project converted to **OfficeFloor function injection**, built with **Maven**. Telephone/E.164 handling is the central theme of the owner-creation pipeline. There is no JSR-303 custom `ConstraintValidator` or custom annotation for telephone; validation is done by (a) a JPA `@Pattern` on the entity and (b) plain logic in OfficeFloor function classes.

## 1. Classes/validators dealing with telephone / E.164

**Core normalizer (the actual E.164 logic):** `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/TelephoneNormalizer.java`
Package-private utility. Strips `[\s()\-]`, keeps a leading `+` + country code if present, otherwise assumes country code `+61` and drops one leading `0`. Requires 8–15 digits after `+`, else returns `null`.
```java
static String toE164(String raw) {
    if (raw == null) return null;
    String cleaned = raw.replaceAll("[\\s()\\-]", "");
    String digits;
    if (cleaned.startsWith("+")) {
        digits = cleaned.substring(1);
    } else {
        String national = cleaned.startsWith("0") ? cleaned.substring(1) : cleaned;
        digits = "61" + national;
    }
    if (!digits.matches("[0-9]{8,15}")) return null;
    return "+" + digits;
}
```

**Entity-level Bean Validation annotation:** in `Owner.java` (see section 4) — `@Pattern(regexp = "^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$", ...)`.

## 2. Where telephone numbers are validated (execution flow)

The `POST /api/owners` pipeline is declared in `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`. Ordered steps relevant to telephone:
- `validate` → `ValidateNewOwner` (presence check)
- `normalizeTelephone` → `NormalizeOwnerTelephone`
- `ensureUniqueTelephone` → `EnsureUniqueTelephone`

**Presence check** — `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/ValidateNewOwner.java` (line 26): `checkPresent("telephone", request.getTelephone(), missing);` — blank/missing telephone → `MissingOwnerFieldsException`.

**Normalization + format validation** — `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/NormalizeOwnerTelephone.java`:
```java
public void service(@Val OwnerFieldsDto request) throws InvalidTelephoneException {
    String raw = request.getTelephone();
    String e164 = TelephoneNormalizer.toE164(raw);
    if (e164 == null) throw new InvalidTelephoneException(raw);
    request.setTelephone(e164);  // mutates shared @Val object
}
```
A number that can't form valid E.164 → `InvalidTelephoneException` → HTTP 400.

**Uniqueness check** — `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/EnsureUniqueTelephone.java`: compares the request's E.164 value against every existing owner's telephone (also normalized via `TelephoneNormalizer.toE164`), throwing `DuplicateTelephoneException` (HTTP 409) on collision.

**Persistence copy** — `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/ApplyOwner.java` (line 13) copies the normalized telephone onto the `Owner` entity.

**Exception → HTTP handlers:**
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/InvalidTelephoneException.java` — message "Telephone cannot be normalized to a valid E.164 number: ...", holds `rejectedValue`.
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/InvalidTelephoneExceptionHandler.java` — responds 400 `ProblemDetail`, detail "The telephone must be a valid E.164 number (a '+' followed by 8 to 15 digits)", sets `rejectedValue`.
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/DuplicateTelephoneException.java` and `.../DuplicateTelephoneExceptionHandler.java` — 409 conflict.
- Wiring: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/escalation/org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation.InvalidTelephoneException.yml` and `...DuplicateTelephoneException.yml` map each exception to its handler.

The JDBC repos (`JdbcOwnerRepositoryImpl.java`, `JdbcPetRepositoryImpl.java`, `JdbcVisitRepositoryImpl.java`) only reference `telephone` as a DB column in SQL/param mapping — no validation logic there.

## 3. Existing tests for telephone / E.164

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceTest.java`** — the one direct telephone test:
```java
/** telephone-country-length: Validate the E.164 telephone's national-number length against its country code ('+61' requ... */
class AcceptanceTest extends AcceptanceBase {
    @Test
    void errorRejectsWrongNationalLength() throws Exception {
        ObjectNode o = ownerNode();
        o.put("telephone", "+61 123");
        createOwner(o).andExpect(status().isBadRequest()); // +61 needs 9 national digits
    }
}
```

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceBase.java`** — black-box base (`@SpringBootTest`, `@AutoConfigureMockMvc`, `@Transactional`, `@WithMockUser` OWNER_ADMIN). Relevant telephone helper (lines 98–104):
```java
/** A unique 10-digit AU mobile ('04XXXXXXXX')... dropping the leading '0' yields 9 national
 *  digits, which is exactly what the E.164 '+61' form and the per-country length rule require. */
protected String uniqueTelephone() {
    return String.format("04%08d", seq());
}
```
`ownerNode()` (line 117) puts this telephone into the default valid payload; `createOwner(...)` POSTs to `/api/owners`. No other test files reference telephone/E.164/phone.

Note: the acceptance test comment describes a `+61`-specific national-length rule (9 national digits), but the current `TelephoneNormalizer` only enforces a generic 8–15 digit total. `+61 123` normalizes to `+61123` (6 digits) which fails the 8-digit minimum, so the test passes coincidentally — there is no country-specific length rule implemented.

## 4. DTO / entity fields holding telephone numbers

**Entity:** `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java` (lines 46–49):
```java
@Column(name = "telephone")
@NotEmpty
@Pattern(regexp = "^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$", message = "Phone number must be E.164 (a '+' followed by 8 to 15 digits)")
private String telephone;
```
(Getter/setter at lines 91–97; also included in `toString()`.)

**DTO:** `OwnerFieldsDto` (used as `@RequestBody` / `@Val` throughout the functions) is **generated at build time** by the `openapi-generator-maven-plugin` from the schema in `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/openapi.yml`. It is not checked into the source tree (no `target/` present). The `telephone` schema (lines 2026–2033, required at line 2062):
```yaml
telephone:
  title: Telephone number
  description: The telephone number of the pet owner.
  type: string
  minLength: 1
  maxLength: 20
  pattern: '^[0-9]*$'
  example: '6085551023'
```
Note the DTO-level `pattern: '^[0-9]*$'` (digits only, no `+`) differs from the entity's E.164 `@Pattern` and from the normalizer output (which produces a leading `+`). The normalizer mutates the DTO's telephone to `+...` form after this input validation.

## 5. Build & test

- **Build tool:** Maven, with wrapper `/home/daniel/sandbox/mvnw` (and `mvnw.cmd`). POM: `/home/daniel/sandbox/pom.xml`, parent `spring-boot-starter-parent`.
- **Key plugins:** `openapi-generator-maven-plugin` 7.23.0 (generatorName `spring`, inputSpec `src/main/resources/openapi.yml`, output to `target/generated-sources/openapi/src/main/java`) generates the DTOs/API interfaces; MapStruct for mapping; `officefloor-rest-spring-boot-4-starter` for the function injection runtime.
- **Run all tests:** `./mvnw test` (from `/home/daniel/sandbox`). Full build incl. DTO generation: `./mvnw verify` or `./mvnw clean package`.
- **Run just the telephone acceptance test:** `./mvnw test -Dtest=AcceptanceTest`.
- Tests use JUnit 5 (`spring-boot-starter-test`, `spring-boot-starter-webmvc-test`, `spring-boot-starter-security-test`) with MockMvc against `POST /api/owners` and `GET /api/owners/{id}`.
- `docker-compose.yml` exists (likely DB) if an integration DB is needed. Project guidance is in `/home/daniel/sandbox/CLAUDE.md` and `/home/daniel/sandbox/AGENTS.md`.

